  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The StarVR One uses a \"fake\" Vive Tracker embedded into the headset which is seen by SteamVR.\nThe tracker causes VRCHAT to believe there is a hip tracker when there is none and causes weird issues with the stance of the avatar(hips forward while standing and crouching while sitting down). You must also calibrate each time you change avatar and when you login.\nA temp solution could be a parameter to ignore Vive Trackers?\nA solution for this would probably also fix it for other hmds that use a \"fake\" Vive Tracker(I'm not sure if Vive Cosmos Elite uses it).\nThank you. I can help to test if needed.",
